sub:assertion {
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/aristotle-ga02-01> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/Claim>;
    dc:description "Animals generate because a living thing cannot be eternal as an individual but can be eternal as a species, which is why there is always a race of men, animals and plants.";
    dc:type "conceptual";
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Generation makes kinds eternal as species, not as individuals";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/context> "Aristotle, On the Generation of Animals (De Generatione Animalium), Book II; translated by Arthur Platt, The Works of Aristotle Translated into English, ed. J. A. Smith and W. D. Ross, Oxford: Clarendon Press, vol. V (1912). Scope: All animals and plants"
}
